invariant: INV-17
file: gcm_avx512.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm_open_avx512 returns without wiping the stack below its frame,
  so the powers of the hash subkey in the kernel's frame, and whatever the
  compiler kept in slots of its own there, stay in the dead frame. Every
  byte the open writes is still right. The script compiles the file for
  x86-64 and requires each entry to call wipe_frame through its pointer,
  and bin/gcm_avx512_equiv_test searches the stack after each entry on a
  CPU with AVX-512.

--- old
    wipe_frame_call();
    avx512_wipe_registers();
}

#endif // CH_CPU_RUNTIME && (__x86_64__ || CH_GCM_AVX512_MODEL)
--- new
    avx512_wipe_registers();
}

#endif // CH_CPU_RUNTIME && (__x86_64__ || CH_GCM_AVX512_MODEL)
